id: pm-xp7ldt
title: update-many ignores an unknown flat update key where a single update refuses it by name
description: "Observed while fixing typed null handling in update-many. runAction('update-many', { options: { ids: [id], bogus: 'x', description: 'changed' } }) changes the description and reports one updated row; the unknown key is dropped without a warning. The same payload through runAction('update') refuses with: Unknown update option \"bogus\". Did you mean \"body\"? No changes were made. The GH-1520 admission check covers native create and update only, so a misspelled bulk field (for example asignee) is silently not applied to any matched row."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[4]: admission,"area:sdk",honesty,update-many
created_at: "2026-11-21T19:34:43.782Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-22T11:39:36.219Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#8fcf1176eceedef40be11ce4"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "runAction update-many refuses an undeclared flat update key by name with the nearest declared key before any row changes, in the flat and nested spellings; Declared aliases, runtime schema fields and extension fields stay accepted; MCP update-many keeps its transport contract; A spec proves parity with the single update refusal for the same key"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: "An unknown update key in an update-many payload is refused by name, as a single update refuses it"
actual_result: The unknown key is dropped and the remaining fields are applied to every matched row
