comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-21T19:34:43.782Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: pm search for 'update-many unknown option key silently ignored' returned the closed GH-1520 item (create and update admission, not bulk) and no open item for the bulk path."
  "2026-11-21T21:42:48.288Z","harness:claude-code","Related shape from the third Codex review of PR 1764: a JSON-decoded options bag with an own __proto__ key loses that key when normalization copies it into a plain object, so neither the unknown-key check nor the typed null scan sees it. The admission check should read the caller's own keys before any copy."
  "2026-11-22T01:53:55.817Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented on branch fix/sdk-admission-scope-identity. dispatchAction now calls assertNativeUpdateManyOptions (src/sdk/runtime/mutation-admission.ts) for a native update-many before the handler runs. It reads the caller's own option keys before any normalization copy, so an own __proto__ key is judged, and refuses an undeclared key with the message, nearest-name hint and typed context a single update gives for the same key. With a nested update record, the record's keys are judged as update options and every outer key must select rows or control the run; an update field left outside is refused with its update.<key> placement instead of being ignored. Finding while writing the spec: the bulk path applies a runtime schema field only when the field is declared for update_many (collectRuntimeUpdateFieldValues in update-many.ts), so a field declared for update alone was also dropped without notice. Admission therefore accepts runtime fields by the update_many declaration, not the update one. MCP transport input returns before the check. Proof: tests/integration/sdk/mutation-admission.integration.spec.ts, case 'refuses an undeclared update-many key by name before any row changes, as a single update does'."
  "2026-11-22T03:03:50.811Z","harness:claude-code","First Codex review findings on the bulk admission, each verified and fixed in the follow-up commit. options.id and list.id passed admission and selected nothing, so the update would have reached every matching row: id is refused with an ids hint and a nested list record admits list selection keys only. A misspelled top-level argument was not judged: the action envelope is now checked and a misplaced field names options.<key>. Outer author, message and force beside a nested update record were admitted but dropped by the normalizer: updateManyOptionsFromFlat now carries them into the record unless the record states its own. output_format and documentAnnotationSnapshot, which the dispatch consumes, were refused: snake_case run and output controls and the annotation snapshot guard are admitted."
  "2026-11-22T03:21:45.475Z","harness:claude-code","Second Codex round on bulk admission, verified and fixed. Selection is now stated in one place: list.status (which the plan overwrites with filterStatus) and a flat ids, limit, offset or filter key beside a list record (which the normalizer drops) are refused by name. A snake_case selector such as filter_status was admitted through the control-key mapping and selected nothing: only output controls are mapped. A list or update value that is an array or a string was read as absent and is refused. An outer force is carried into a nested update record only when it is the literal true, since a carried string would be read as truthy, and a top-level force, which the bulk handler never read, is refused with its options.force placement. CLI input-source options (bodyFile, stdinJson and their kin) are no longer admitted as bulk fields. The first round's allowlist for nested list keys rejected selectors the list runner consumes (excludeTerminal, alias spellings, workspace list fields): it is replaced by the single rule that id is refused, leaving the list record to the list contract."
  "2026-11-22T03:40:39.296Z","harness:claude-code","Third Codex round, verified and fixed. The flat-selector conflict check matched any key starting with filter, so a runtime schema field such as filter_region declared for update_many was refused beside a list record: the check now uses the exact flat selector keys. An undefined inner author, message or force overwrote the carried outer value through spread order: carried values are applied after the nested record."
  "2026-11-22T09:29:02.736Z","harness:claude-code","Review round on head 7e0844634. (1) Gates (static) failed on ESLint complexity 21 and cognitive complexity 25 in assertNativeUpdateManyOptions; the function is now a sequence of four named checks (updateManyFieldKeys, assertBulkContainers, assertListRecord, assertOuterKeysBesideNestedUpdate) with one refusal builder. (2) Greptile P1: a misspelled key inside the list record (list.assigneee) passed admission, was carried unread by normalizeListOptions, and the update reached every row the remaining selectors matched. The list record's keys are now judged against the list contract (every flag and alias of LIST_FILTER_FLAG_CONTRACTS in camelCase, a negated flag under its positive key) plus list filters of runtime schema fields; anything else is refused by name with the nearest declared key. That also refuses a pre-normalized key such as noNotes and a snake_case key such as tree_depth, both of which were dropped. Spec rows added to mutation-admission.integration.spec.ts, with an accepted row covering type, assignee, notes false, sort and a runtime list filter.\n"
  "2026-11-22T11:02:10.896Z","harness:claude-code","Second review round on head 38d735f67 (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh and Greptile). The list-record allowlist was derived from CLI flags alone, which was wrong in both directions. It refused selectors the bulk planner reads: the reader aliases assignee_filter and tree_depth, and the SDK-only selectors excludeTerminal, lifecycleBucket and dependencyBlocked. It admitted the intent keys for and tokenBudget, which bound a list command's page through applyContextIntentProjection but are not applied by buildUpdateManyPlan, so a caller expecting a budget-sized page would have updated every matching row. The allowlist is now the declared list flags plus every key of LIST_COMMANDER_STRING_OPTION_CONTRACTS plus the three SDK-only selectors; for and tokenBudget are refused with a list.limit hint. The spec accepts a list record using the aliases and SDK-only selectors and refuses the two intent keys.\n"
  "2026-11-22T11:39:36.218Z","harness:claude-code","Third review round on head 59164549e (Codex). The list-record admission now checks the runtime schema before refusing a list-command-only key, so a tracker that registers a list field named token_budget keeps its filter; list.all is refused with a filterStatus all hint like list.status, because the bulk planner never applies it. Projection keys such as fields stay accepted: the planner clears them and they do not change which rows are written.\n"
