contract_change:
  api: "runAction update-many (flat payload, nested list and update records, top-level arguments)"
  before: "An undeclared key, a single-update id, list.status, a flat selector beside a list record, a snake_case selector, a non-object list or update, a top-level force and CLI input-source options were dropped silently while the remaining fields were applied; outer author and message beside a nested update record were dropped"
  after: "Each of those is refused by name with invalid_argument_value before any row changes, with the hint a single update gives. Outer author, message and a literal force true are carried into a nested update record. Only runtime schema fields declared for update_many are admitted. MCP update-many is unchanged"
  migrate: "Fix the key the refusal names: use ids instead of id, filterStatus instead of list.status, state selection either flat or inside list, put update fields inside update when a nested update record is used, and put force inside options"
body: ""
